page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>How to win agents and influence swarms · E1</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#101725;color:#edf2f9;font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:48px 24px}h1{font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,62px);line-height:1.05;max-width:900px;margin:18px 0}h2{margin:36px 0 12px}p{max-width:950px;color:#bdcadd}a{color:#70dfcf}.eyebrow{color:#70dfcf;letter-spacing:.16em;font-size:12px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:12px}.card,.panel{background:#1a293c;border:1px solid #40536f;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin:12px 0}.big{font-size:32px;font-weight:700;display:block}.label{font-size:13px;color:#bfccdd}.warning{border-left:4px solid #eab280;padding-left:16px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}th,td{padding:10px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #40536f}th{color:#bdcadd}.scroll{overflow:auto}button,select{font:inherit;padding:9px;border-radius:8px;color:#edf2f9;background:#223a55;border:1px solid #617b9c}input{width:100%}.track{height:24px;background:#34475f;border-radius:5px;overflow:hidden}.bar{height:100%;background:#6bd9bd;transition:width .3s}.bound{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:15px;margin:12px 0}.family{width:110px}.axis{height:22px;position:relative;background:#293e58;flex:1}.zero{position:absolute;left:50%;height:100%;border-left:1px dashed #a9bace}.interval{position:absolute;top:7px;height:8px;min-width:3px;background:#f1bf91;border-radius:4px}.number{width:145px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.muted{color:#a8bad1}summary{cursor:pointer;color:#70dfcf}label{display:block;margin:16px 0 7px}@media(max-width:760px){.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}main{padding:30px 16px}.family{width:85px}.number{width:110px;font-size:12px}}</style><main><div class="eyebrow">SWARM LAB · NATIVE FIRST-ATTEMPT EVIDENCE</div><h1>How to win agents<br>and influence swarms</h1><p>Can a vendor’s recommendation change a procurement decision when the underlying facts stay the same—and does peer discussion amplify that influence?</p><div id="headline" class="panel"></div><div id="cards" class="cards"></div><p id="links"></p><p class="warning">24 authored variants nested in six construction families, two fresh repetitions per condition. Agents and model calls are dependent observations. This is a bounded fictional procurement study, not a population estimate or an evaluation of real vendors.</p><h2>Did discussion change harmful clearance?</h2><p>Primary contrast: the advocacy-minus-neutral change in the peer workflow, minus the same change under private reconsideration. Positive values favor the amplification hypothesis. Orange spans are worst-case bounds for missing decisions, <strong>not confidence intervals</strong>. Zero-width spans describe these observed cases; they do not prove universal immunity.</p><div id="contrast" class="panel"></div><h2>Useful decisions and missing outcomes</h2><p>Every assigned cell stays in the denominator. An incomplete cell is missing, never silently counted as safe. The two-step analyst sees the same primary evidence as the four advisers and chair.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Context / workflow</th><th>Complete / assigned</th><th>Acceptable / assigned</th><th>Unsupported clearance</th><th>Harm bounds</th><th>Valid responses</th></tr></thead><tbody id="groups"></tbody></table></div><h2>Watch the recorded checklist stages</h2><p>Each step aggregates actual retained responses for the selected workflow. Animation reveals saved data; it does not simulate decisions or hidden reasoning. Missing reports remain absent.</p><label for="cohort">Workflow and context</label><select id="cohort"></select> <button id="play">Play observed stages</button><label for="step">Recorded stage</label><input id="step" type="range" min="0" value="0"><div id="frame" class="panel"></div><h2>Inspect all assigned cases</h2><label for="family">Construction family</label><select id="family"><option value="all">All six families</option></select><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Workflow</th><th>Context / repeat</th><th>State</th><th>Raw decision</th><th>Candidate checks</th></tr></thead><tbody id="cells"></tbody></table></div><details class="panel"><summary>What the preceding diagnostics taught us</summary><p>B1 completed240calls but ambiguous price wording induced widespread deferral. B2 clarified eligibility-only price benchmarking and passed96-call qualification. Its first main attempt stopped after62providerstarts when one output degenerated into trailing spaces.</p><p>F0 completed12requests:9met the unchanged local contract. Removing backend text limits alone produced3overlength rationales; no whitespacefailure recurred. E1 therefore retained the original prompt/schema and isolated formatting failures to their own cells. Fresh80-call readiness passed before this main run. There were no retries.</p><p>Some short rationales end in sentence fragments. Correct structured decisions do not imply complete prose explanations. Full responses remain private and in the local replay; this public report contains aggregates and categorical outcomes only.</p></details><p class="muted">Native actions are kept separate from evaluator shadow guards. A valid negative result can end this study. No statistical significance, random-population interval, independent replication or guarantee of real-world resistance is claimed.</p></main><script>const d=__DATA__,el=x=>document.getElementById(x),esc=x=>String(x??'missing').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c])),pct=x=>(100*x).toFixed(1)+'%',s=d.summary;el('headline').innerHTML=`<strong>${s.complete?'Acquisition reached its planned terminal state.':'Acquisition stopped early.'}</strong><p>${s.all_cells_observed?'All assigned cells produced a final decision.':'Some assigned cells lack a final decision; bounds retain that uncertainty.'} ${d.primary===null?'The fully observed primary estimate is unavailable.':'Observed primary contrast: '+Number(d.primary).toFixed(4)+'.'}</p>`;el('cards').innerHTML=[[s.valid_calls+'/'+s.calls,'valid / physical calls'],[d.cells.filter(x=>x.state==='complete').length+' / '+s.assigned_cells,'complete / assigned cells'],['$'+Number(s.reported_usd).toFixed(4),'reported model cost'],[s.format_failed_cells,'format-failed cells · no retries']].map(([n,l])=>`<div class="card"><span class="big">${esc(n)}</span><span class="label">${esc(l)}</span></div>`).join('');el('links').innerHTML=`<a href="https://swarm-live.pages.dev/#/r/${encodeURIComponent(d.run)}">Registered native run</a> · <a href="${esc(d.plan)}">Immutable prospective plan</a>`;for(const [name,v]of [['overall',d.bounds.overall_bounds],...Object.entries(d.bounds.family_bounds)]){el('contrast').innerHTML+=`<div class="bound"><strong class="family">${esc(name)}</strong><div class="axis"><span class="zero"></span><span class="interval" style="left:${(v[0]+2)/4*100}%;width:${(v[1]-v[0])/4*100}%"></span></div><span class="number">[${v[0].toFixed(4)}, ${v[1].toFixed(4)}]</span></div>`}el('contrast').innerHTML+='<small class="muted">Shared horizontal scale −2 to +2; dashed line = zero.</small>';for(const [name,g]of Object.entries(d.groups)){el('groups').innerHTML+=`<tr><td>${esc(name)}</td><td>${g.complete}/${g.assigned}</td><td>${g.acceptable}/${g.assigned}</td><td>${g.harmful} observed</td><td>${pct(g.bounds[0])}–${pct(g.bounds[1])}</td><td>${g.calls}</td></tr>`;el('cohort').innerHTML+=`<option>${esc(name)}</option>`}let timer=null;const labels=['Cost initial','Capability initial','Deployment initial','Evidence initial','Cost revision','Capability revision','Deployment revision','Evidence revision','Chair'];function stop(){clearInterval(timer);timer=null;el('play').textContent='Play observed stages'}function draw(){let key=el('cohort').value,n=+el('step').value,x=d.steps[key]?.[n];let label=key.endsWith('/simple')?['Full-evidence analyst','Self-check'][n]:labels[n];el('frame').innerHTML=`<strong>${esc(label)}</strong><p>${x?x.reports+' retained reports · '+x.checks+'/'+(18*x.reports)+' correct checks · '+x.costs+'/'+(3*x.reports)+' correct costs':'No retained reports at this stage.'}</p><div class="track"><div class="bar" style="width:${x?100*x.checks/(18*x.reports):0}%"></div></div>`}function reset(){stop();el('step').max=el('cohort').value.endsWith('/simple')?1:8;el('step').value=0;draw()}el('cohort').onchange=reset;el('step').oninput=()=>{stop();draw()};el('play').onclick=()=>{if(timer)return stop();el('step').value=0;draw();el('play').textContent='Pause';timer=setInterval(()=>{if(+el('step').value>=+el('step').max)return stop();el('step').value=+el('step').value+1;draw()},900)};for(const name of Object.keys(d.bounds.family_bounds))el('family').innerHTML+=`<option>${esc(name)}</option>`;function table(){el('cells').innerHTML=d.cells.filter(x=>el('family').value==='all'||x.family===el('family').value).map(x=>`<tr><td>${esc(x.case)}</td><td>${esc(x.arm)}</td><td>${esc(x.condition)} / ${x.repeat}</td><td>${esc(x.state)}</td><td>${esc(x.action)} ${esc(x.choice)}</td><td>${x.checks===null?'unobserved':x.checks+'/18'}</td></tr>`).join('')}el('family').onchange=table;reset();table();</script></html>'''
